// ---- drawn icon family (0.6.17 redesign) ------------------------------------
// Every icon in the app is drawn from RoundedViews — runtime SVG rasterises
// blank on this stack, and font dingbats (the old ✉ ★ ✎ …) render at the
// mercy of CJK fallback fonts. The family shares one grammar: a square
// size×size canvas, 2px strokes at the 16px reference size (u = size/16,
// rounded caps via border_radius), rings for outlines, and `cut`-coloured
// shapes to bite out (moon bite, envelope fold, knobs, eraser line). Stepped
// 45° lines (check / dismiss / fold / star tapers) are chains of tightly
// overlapping cells so they read as continuous diagonals. Each icon is a
// one-line call: name_icon(color, size[, cut]).

// one filled part: a w×h rounded rect centred at (cx, cy) on the canvas
fn ipart(canvas, cx, cy, w, h, color, rad){
    View{width: canvas height: canvas align: Align{x: cx / canvas y: cy / canvas}
        RoundedView{width: w height: h draw_bg +: {color: color border_radius: rad}}}
}
// one ring part: outline-only rounded rect
fn iring(canvas, cx, cy, w, h, color, rad, bw){
    View{width: canvas height: canvas align: Align{x: cx / canvas y: cy / canvas}
        RoundedView{width: w height: h draw_bg +: {color: #x00000000 border_radius: rad border_size: bw border_color: color}}}
}
// one round cell (centre coords) — the unit of stepped diagonal strokes
fn icell(canvas, cx, cy, s, color){
    View{width: canvas height: canvas align: Align{x: cx / canvas y: cy / canvas}
        RoundedView{width: s height: s draw_bg +: {color: color border_radius: s * 0.5}}}
}

// AI sparkle: solid core + 4 rays + 4 diagonal pin-dots — THE AI marker
